Always refer to the latest documentation here: https://sdk.vercel.ai/docs/ai-sdk-core

- Use the Vercel AI SDK UI for implementing streaming chat UI.
- Use the Vercel AI SDK Core to interact with language models.
- Use the Vercel AI SDK RSC and Stream Helpers to stream and help with the generations.
- Implement proper error handling for AI responses and model switching.
- Implement fallback mechanisms for when an AI model is unavailable.
- Handle rate limiting and quota exceeded scenarios gracefully.
- Provide clear error messages to users when AI interactions fail.
- Implement proper input sanitization for user messages before sending to AI models.
- Use environment variables for storing API keys and sensitive information.

Sample Implementation
import { streamText } from 'ai';
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';

// Allow responses up to 5 minutes
export const maxDuration = 300;

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  try {
    const { messages } = await req.json();

    const result = streamText({
      model: openai('o3-mini'),
      messages,
      // Configure reasoning effort for optimal performance
      providerOptions: {
        openai: { 
          reasoningEffort: 'medium' // Default to medium for balanced performance
        },
      },
    });

    return result.toDataStreamResponse();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('[Research API Error]:', error);
    return new Response('An error occurred during research processing', { status: 500 });
  }
}